```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <markdown.h>

/**
 * Converts markdown text to HTML.
 *
 * @param markdownText The markdown text to convert.
 * @return The HTML text.
 */
std::string markdownToHtml(const std::string& markdownText) {
    markdown::MarkdownIn markdown(markdownText);
    markdown::MarkdownOut htmlOut;

    markdown.markdown(markdownIn, htmlOut);

    return htmlOut.c_str();
}

int main() {
    std::string markdownText = "# Hello, World!";
    std::string htmlText = markdownToHtml(markdownText);

    std::cout << "Markdown: " << markdownText << std::endl;
    std::cout << "HTML: " << htmlText << std::endl;

    return 0;
}
```

This code uses the markdown library to convert markdown text to HTML. The `markdownToHtml` function takes a reference to a `std::string` containing markdown text, converts it to HTML, and returns the HTML text as a `std::string`.

Please note that you need to install the markdown library to compile this code. You can install it using your package manager or by downloading it from the official website.

Also, this code assumes that the markdown text is well-formed and does not contain any invalid markdown syntax. If you need to handle invalid markdown syntax, you may need to add error checking code to the `markdownToHtml` function.

